   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to increasing the number of visits with no prior notice that can be made to a facility per year",
    "basePrintNo": "S5098",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5098-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16.11, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5098\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to\nincreasing the number of visits with no prior notice that can be made\nto a facility per year\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo increase the number of unannounced inspections conducted at\nfacilities operated and/or licensed by the Office of People with\nDevelopmental Disabilities (OPWDD) to a minimum of two per year.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends subdivision (a) of section 16.11 of the\nmental hygiene law to increase the number of unannounced inspections\nof facilities from a minimum of one to a minimum of two per year.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSubdivision (a) of section 16.11 of the mental hygiene law states that\nat least one inspection of a facility be made without prior notice to\na facility.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill maintains the same number of inspections of a facility at a\nminimum of two per year; however it would make them unannounced.\nCurrently, only one unannounced visit per year of OPWDD facilities is\nrequired by law. This bill also allows members of a board of visitors\nand other individuals, if approved by the Commissioner, to accompany\ninspectors and serve as independent monitors during the State's\nperiodic visitations and inspections. By having unannounced visits and\ninspections, facilities will maintain inspection standards throughout\nthe year, providing the best care to the developmentally disabled.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately\n\n",
